{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And it shall come to pass that he cries out to Me.</b> He means: if this rich man shuts his ear to the outcry of the poor man, let him not imagine that thereby the poor man's hope is lost — rather, 'when he cries out <b>to Me</b> and I hear,' for if he is cruel, I am not like him; rather, ״וְשָׁמַעְתִּי כִּי חַנּוּן אָנִי״ — 'and I hear, for I am gracious.' Or he may say: from Me you shall see, and so shall you do — by an a fortiori inference."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:22:24.565152362Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}